\title{tabarenaR: TabArena evaluation entirely in R}
\description{
The package reproduces the TabArena benchmark pipeline in R:
}
\details{
\enumerate{
\item \code{\link[=ta_tasks]{ta_tasks()}} lists the 51 TabArena-v0.1 tasks (OpenML task ids, problem
type, metric, number of splits).
\item \code{\link[=ta_load_task]{ta_load_task()}} downloads a task's data and its official outer
cross-validation splits from OpenML and caches them locally.
\item \code{\link[=ta_learner]{ta_learner()}} wraps any pair of R functions \code{train(X, y, ctx)} and
\code{predict(model, X, ctx)}.
\item \code{\link[=ta_evaluate]{ta_evaluate()}} runs the learner on the requested tasks and splits and
scores it with the official metric of each task (1 - ROC AUC for binary
classification, log loss for multiclass, RMSE for regression).
\item \code{\link[=ta_results]{ta_results()}} loads the published per-task results of the leaderboard
methods (a bundled snapshot of the paper results, or the live results
that back the online leaderboard).
\item \code{\link[=ta_leaderboard]{ta_leaderboard()}} and \code{\link[=ta_elo]{ta_elo()}} compute the Bradley-Terry Elo with
task-level bootstrap confidence intervals, calibrated so that
\code{RF (default)} sits at 1000, plus win rate, mean rank, harmonic rank,
normalized score, improvability and timing columns, mirroring the
official implementation.
\item \code{\link[=ta_benchmark]{ta_benchmark()}} chains steps 4 to 6 in one call.
}

Downloads are cached under \code{tools::R_user_dir("tabarenaR", "cache")};
set \code{options(tabarenaR.cache_dir = "...")} or the environment variable
\code{TABARENA_R_CACHE} to change the location.
